{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>YHWH will see.</b> Abraham says: thus <b>YHWH will see</b>, and it will be for me a sign that I fulfilled His commandment, for I know that <b>they will say today</b> in many places: on <b>the mountain of YHWH</b> where Abraham led his son there — will He appear to us if he can honor Him to slaughter his son? And when they see me returning with my son, they will say that I denied El above and rejected His words, and they will not believe that it was from HaShem, the cause. But the Holy One, blessed be He, will see that I did not rebel against His words, and it will be for me a sign."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:19.149762157Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}